 so  wrong  um from a young age and then you know as  a teenager  as you start to develop and you know  start to have these feelings and and you  know start to kind of realize more and  more what sexuality is i was like oh no  like this is like a  real thing i fought it like through my  teen years until finally i just accepted  it in my late teens and i was like no  like this is a part of me this is  like this is this is me it's just been a  very complex complicated journey but i'm  just so glad to finally be  finally accepting of who i am and not  not think there's anything wrong with it  well we have a mutual friend by the name  of priyanka  you know priyanka shared her support for  you online your fans were so supportive  what did it mean to kind of get that  feedback from your fan base  and people like canada's drag race  winner it's funny because i i knew  her before she ever did drag and so  um it's kind of like this full circle  moment where i just came back around and  i got to tell her like i remember  watching you on  drag race and saying you know just be  gay just be gay  and that was just a huge inspiration for  me to come out too because i was like no  there's no point in hiding it anymore  i was not expecting the post to to do  what it did like there's hundreds and  hundreds of comments of people  just having all that all that support  from people who are also in the  community too that's that's another  thing i don't i  didn't know too many people from within  the community but to  realize all the support within the  community as well is just incredible so  it's more than i could have ever asked  for your music has really taken off  i think i saw that in my head had over  10 million streams worldwide that is  incredible  now that you have this new sense of  freedom is that going to give you a  chance to  feel um not that your music wasn't 100  authentic before but is it going to take  your music to a  new place would you say a hundred  percent  and um you know my music yeah like  before it was it was i was i was playing  it safe in a way it was authentic and it  was stories that i created and obviously  was very proud of but now i feel like  going forward i'm actually  like now i can just go into sessions and  write exactly what i feel and  i think i was trying to discover who i  was at that time too so it wasn't fully  you know authentic to who i am now  to me there's now no boundaries before i  was afraid of being you know too  feminine or too like flamboyant or  something or two to whatever it was  whatever the label was  now i can just create whatever i want to  and that just opens up the sky and the  universe  and everything and i'm just excited  about it so i'm just kind of starting  into that creative path now which is  really exciting  oh hey there if you want more lgbtq news  and exclusive interviews click  subscribe or watch these videos
 

